    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/activity-log.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Activity log — what an agent did, kept out of the graph",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-09-19:\n\n> an agent whenever it starts or ends a task or has a log message, they\n> should add an entry to a log entry in the trash. […] by default commit\n> audit log to git data store is turned off - need explict like (cpature log\n> when agent runs this workflow).\n\n## The role is mechanical",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-19"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/activity-log.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The role is mechanical",
      "prov:value": "`work-plan` and `corpus`, and this is deliberately the same shape rather than\na new one. A mechanical role is still a real role (owner, 2026-10-16): this\nskill is its **contract** — the shape of an entry and where it goes — and the\n`actedUpon` flag that once exempted it from `role-has-actor` is retired.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-16"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/activity-log.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "What an entry points at — `references[]` is OPEN",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-09-19:\n\n> log should be rich schema including references to discussion/chats, cmn\n> execution logs, etc.\n\n**The `etc.` is the specification, not a trailing-off.** A closed list is\nwrong within a week — the interesting thing to reference is whatever the work\ntouched, and nobody enumerates that in advance. So `kind` is an open string\nwith a KNOWN SET",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-19"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/activity-log.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "What an entry points at — `references[]` is OPEN",
      "prov:value": "> `cmn` was read as **command**. There is no CMMN in this codebase — the\n> process standards here are BPMN and DMN — and \"execution logs\" pairs with a\n> command. If CMMN was meant, it arrives as `kind: \"case\"` with **no schema\n> change**, which is exactly what an open list buys.\n\n### Command execution has its own shape, and no output field"
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/activity-log.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Turning it on — `<cat-harness.processes:log capture=\"on\"/>` on the process",
      "prov:value": "Owner: *\"need explicit like (capture log when agent runs this workflow).\"*\nThat is a declaration on the **process**, parsed at load and **throwing on a\nvalue the engine cannot honour**, exactly as `<cat-harness.processes:bean op>` does. A diagram\nasking for a mode that does not exist must not load and quietly log nothing —\nworse here than elsewhere, because the missing artefact *is* the record."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/activity-log.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "It is never published",
      "prov:value": "`fsh-guts/logs/` is inside `fsh-guts/`, which `UNPUBLISHED_GRAPH_TYPOLOGIES`\nstrips from every published graph — the kind, the directory, the skill and\nevery edge naming them (bean `folio-assistant-uv09`,\n[`kg-export`](../../../skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md)).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean folio-assistant-uv09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/activity-log.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "What not to log",
      "prov:value": "a bean says what is\n  being worked on and what it waits on. An agent that logs instead of\n  claiming is the 2026-09-18 unclaimed-work failure wearing a new hat.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-18"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-18"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
